        fp: "A customer entered a high-end specialty electronics boutique. An employee had just finished mopping a section of the polished marble floor near the checkout counter, leaving a visible, wet puddle of soapy water. In violation of the store's safety manual, the employee failed to place any warning signs or cones around the wet area. As the customer walked toward the counter, he was looking directly at his smartphone screen reading a text message and stepped directly into the puddle. The customer slipped, fell backward, and fractured his wrist. In a pure comparative fault jurisdiction, the jury determined that: (1) the customer suffered $50,000 in total damages; (2) the boutique was 60% at fault for failing to post warning signs; and (3) the customer was 40% at fault for failing to pay attention to where he was walking.",
